WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.860
A rooftop in Nepal. A class of fifteen year olds.

00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:08.600
In my hand, a plastic bottle full of water, with holes near the bottom.

00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:09.790
Water streams out.

00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:15.090
I tell them: if Einstein is right, the water will stop the moment I let go.

00:00:15.090 --> 00:00:18.420
Before anything happens, every student must predict.

00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:22.870
Then I release the bottle. For the whole fall, the streams vanish.

00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:25.950
Why? The bottle and the water fall together.

00:00:25.950 --> 00:00:29.810
Inside the falling bottle, the water has no weight to push it out.

00:00:29.810 --> 00:00:34.210
That is free fall, and it is the heart of Einstein's equivalence principle.

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:40.640
Predict, observe, explain. A physics lesson that costs one bottle, and that nobody forgets.

